MinGW g++ 15.2 implements thread_local with emulated TLS: every prof::count() site in the FORGE_PROF build calls __emutls_get_address, even with Profile=false (the null check needs the TLS value).
forge_s08fix_OFF.exe: call __emutls_get_address sites: 11; references to current_bank: 0
forge_s08fix_ON.exe: call __emutls_get_address sites: 35; references to current_bank: 24
Example (ON exe, start of forge::nnue::evaluate): load .refptr.__emutls_v._ZN5forge4prof12current_bankE, call __emutls_get_address, test the bank pointer, add 1 to the counter, setb/or the overflow flag.
